                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "6f38ebec-7813-41a3-a546-496915ced5e5",
                        "entry_id": "a3fbaab6-0a72-3226-bf4b-48c2cb2196a2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "domesticités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0fc29d2c-f5c8-3ef1-8ded-b604e897b678",
                        "entry_id": "a3fbaab6-0a72-3226-bf4b-48c2cb2196a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Condition d’une personne qui est au service d’une autre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dadbeb70-b750-4be6-9e96-d1995c0a69a8",
                                "sense_id": "0fc29d2c-f5c8-3ef1-8ded-b604e897b678",
                                "text": "Elle sanglotait, elle aussi. Elle laissa tomber, sur la poitrine de son maître, sa tête grise, sa face usée par sa longue domesticité."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b056426d-3678-3694-9a9d-ef525e2e4fa8",
                        "entry_id": "a3fbaab6-0a72-3226-bf4b-48c2cb2196a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Tous les domestiques d’une maison."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "collectively"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7a16c8a8-acc1-4f25-9def-3af56d4d4161",
                                "sense_id": "b056426d-3678-3694-9a9d-ef525e2e4fa8",
                                "text": "La domesticité d’un château, d’un palais."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b81b2c8-295e-472e-8084-c7549291a5ed",
                                "sense_id": "b056426d-3678-3694-9a9d-ef525e2e4fa8",
                                "text": "Un spectacle poignant, ces morceaux de grands d’Espagne dans le lustre et le ciel de lit. C’est aussi pour cela que j’ai congédié toute la domesticité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89c3b40c-766b-496f-8a59-939e549b8534",
                                "sense_id": "b056426d-3678-3694-9a9d-ef525e2e4fa8",
                                "text": "La maison Péricourt comprenait une domesticité nombreuse, à quoi il fallait ajouter des extras embauchés pour la journée."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fd03b504-41e3-37c8-a2a4-66bbff64b8ea",
                        "entry_id": "a3fbaab6-0a72-3226-bf4b-48c2cb2196a2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Condition des animaux apprivoisés, par opposition à ceux qui demeurent dans l’état sauvage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d46acb3-4b1f-48e5-b830-6b02276bcd76",
                                "sense_id": "fd03b504-41e3-37c8-a2a4-66bbff64b8ea",
                                "text": "La Girafe dans son pays natal, broute la sommité des arbres, […] : ce qui a décidé de son changement d’habitudes, ce sont les premiers mois de son éducation en domesticité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "19c96f88-0280-42be-91e2-7c147195dfcc",
                                "sense_id": "fd03b504-41e3-37c8-a2a4-66bbff64b8ea",
                                "text": "Puis il le passa à un de ses aides, nouveau et timide, qui exprimait l’effroi qu’il ressentait en roulant en tous sens des regards furieux et montrait l’agitation d’une bête captive dans les premières heures de sa domesticité."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24fc982e-5347-4a18-bcc3-62f5022eb4d8",
                        "source_entry_id": "a3fbaab6-0a72-3226-bf4b-48c2cb2196a2",
                        "target_lang_word": "domesticity",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "domesticity",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61c9c879-3fd9-3e1c-920d-96d6dab1e1cf",
                                        "entry_id": "48183280-2356-324e-b037-f3a0640fdc09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Life at home; homelife."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d76c8530-190c-44a9-aa18-575882c1afdd",
                                                "sense_id": "61c9c879-3fd9-3e1c-920d-96d6dab1e1cf",
                                                "text": "The Neolithic of 8000 to 6000 B.C. is in the sign of Cancer, a feminine sign associated with domesticity, retentiveness, and sentiment."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c66ec689-da4d-3606-9520-4eba86316726",
                                        "entry_id": "48183280-2356-324e-b037-f3a0640fdc09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Domestic chores; housework."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "in-plural",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d486e98a-0508-431f-baaf-6d85d1c5a3e4",
                                                "sense_id": "c66ec689-da4d-3606-9520-4eba86316726",
                                                "text": "Besides the jar of contrast there came to her a chill self-reproach that she had not returned sooner, to help her mother in these domesticities, instead of indulging herself out-of-doors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3b0a7e35-521c-33d0-96d9-648f746a8da6",
                                        "entry_id": "48183280-2356-324e-b037-f3a0640fdc09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Affection for the home and its material comforts."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2ec85142-0c20-42a2-a28c-8856d0ef591f",
                                                "sense_id": "3b0a7e35-521c-33d0-96d9-648f746a8da6",
                                                "text": "As we have seen, Browning renovates her life-after-divorce by framing her domesticity in increasingly autoerotic terms. With her sensuous boudoir, lust for furniture, love affair with houses, and espousal of baked goods, hers is an appetitive domesticity geared to self-pleasure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
